<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

	<!--
		Xenotypes that carry BOTH vanilla non-senescent and Big and Small's Unliving gene drop the vanilla one, so they
		stay valid once the exclusion patch in this same folder makes the two mutually exclusive.

		Why these live here rather than with their own mods' patches: the exclusion tag is only applied when Vampires
		and the Undead is ABSENT, which is what this folder's loadFolders gate checks. The original had the Races
		removal firing whenever Big and Small - Races was active and the Lamias one behind a Royalty check, neither of
		which matches that condition. With Vampires and the Undead installed both used to strip non-senescent from
		xenotypes that nothing had made conflict, which is a plain nerf. Moving them here ties them to the patch that
		creates the need, so the two can no longer drift apart.
		The mod gates sit on <li> nodes inside a sequence, not on the <Operation> itself: RimWorld reads MayRequire only
		on list elements.

		Vanilla's gene has the confusing defName DiseaseFree but is labelled "non-senescent" and prevents chronic
		age-related conditions. VU_Unliving makes its carrier immune to the same six: carcinoma, heart attack,
		dementia, Alzheimer's, asthma and artery blockage. The duplication is exact.

		Verified against the current 1.6 releases: six Big and Small xenotypes carry both genes. Four are the Races ones
		below, one is the Lamias viper prototype, and the sixth is the Revenant from Vampires and the Undead, which
		needs nothing because it only exists in the very case where this folder does not load.
	-->
	<Operation Class="PatchOperationSequence">
		<operations>
			<li Class="PatchOperationRemove" MayRequire="RedMattis.BigSmall">
				<xpath>Defs/XenotypeDef[defName="BS_Hearthguard" or defName="BS_Hearthdoll" or defName="BS_PilotableFleshGolem" or defName="BS_FleshGolemServant"]/genes/li[text()="DiseaseFree"]</xpath>
			</li>
			<li Class="PatchOperationRemove" MayRequire="RedMattis.LamiasAndOtherSnakes">
				<xpath>Defs/XenotypeDef[defName="BS_ViperPrototypeBiomecha"]/genes/li[text()="DiseaseFree"]</xpath>
			</li>
		</operations>
	</Operation>

</Patch>
